{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development would result in a loss of a large family-sized unit, which is a housing type in high demand within the Borough and of which local policies seek to preserve. Officers are not able to support the principle of the proposed development. As such, the proposal is considered unacceptable and contrary to the following policy: &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- National Planning Policy Framework (DLUHC, 2023); and&lt;br&gt;- Policy DMH5 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September, 2024).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed HMO, by reason of increased coming and goings, would potentially increase activity level, which would consequently lead to additional levels of noise/disturbance at the property. This is considered to have a negative impact on neighbouring amenity in this street of family housing and in turn the health and wellbeing of neighbouring residents. As such the proposal is contrary to the following: &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- National Planning Policy Framework (DLUHC, 2023);&lt;br&gt;- Policies D13 and D14 of the London Plan (March 2021); and &lt;br&gt;- Policies DMD1 and DMSI3 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September, 2024).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development would result in inadequate living conditions to prospective occupants on the site, by having undersized bedrooms and communal area, and a lack of storage space, which is contrary to the following planning policies: &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- National Planning Policy Framework (DLUHC, 2023);&lt;br&gt;- Policy D6 of the London Plan (March 2021); and&lt;br&gt;-&amp;nbsp;London Plan Guidance: Housing Design Standards (GLA, June 2023).&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
